1
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,277
You monsters!

2
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,240
Don't turn your backs on me!

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,830
Find it!

4
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:15,640
I'll favor this one!

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,520
Hamon Boba Launcher!

6
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:37,380
Thank you.

7
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:06,200
Thank you.

8
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:49,020
be

9
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,020
continued...

10
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,880
He, he popped them all.

11
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:23,740
How on earth did he do that?

12
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,136
That's not his hair.

13
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:28,377
Those are wires attached to
his head he's manipulating.

14
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:31,537
He popped my bubbles with
the wind that they created.

15
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:35,600
But then that means they were
designed to be anti-Harmon weapons.

16
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,117
Somehow they're already familiar
with the principles of Harmon.

17
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:44,120
They must have faced Harmon at
some point over 2,000 years ago!

18
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,200
What is that?

19
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:49,833
What's happening to the air around them?

20
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,480
Caesar, look out! Get down!

21
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,620
What the...?

22
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,420
Cover your eyes!

23
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,697
That wasn't just wind,

24
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:03,427
it was the aftermath of a powerful
vortex that's still active!

25
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,330
Caesar!

26
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:09,640
These humans know Hamon.

27
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:14,253
I thought we destroyed all the members
of the Hamon tribe 2,000 years ago.

28
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:18,204
And yet, here they are, ready to
welcome us at our own awakening.

29
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,550
Damn.

30
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:24,880
You killed him.

31
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,720
You killed my friend.

32
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,920
Do you think losing an eye will stop me?

33
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:40,397
stop why are you laughing what's so
funny you all have memorized your humble

34
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:43,477
handbook very well you always say the same

35
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,617
thing it was that way when we crossed from

36
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:50,657
the western continent and it is that way
now still do you think losing an arm or

37
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:55,297
an eye or a leg will stop me how dare you
take my friend's life don't you know how

38
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:58,017
much i loved him that's why we laugh

39
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:02,517
human you you bastards ignore him we're on

40
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,297
a quest to find the stone what where

41
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:11,537
are you going face me cowards you're most

42
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:16,277
vulnerable in your throat and your lungs
we know that if you can't breathe then your

43
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:21,400
hormone is rendered useless but because
i cannot resist a worthy opponent hear me

44
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:25,577
i shall spare you because i
long for the opportunity to

45
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:29,577
meet you again when you are
stronger the next time we meet

46
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:32,977
i want to admire your strength
i want you to become worthy

47
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:36,920
of my time so that i might
destroy you with great honor

48
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:50,220
it appears that he was the only
hamon user let's move Ahem!

49
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:58,247
Sorry, I just can't seem
to shake this cough.

50
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,777
Maybe it's the hormone
training that's making me ill.

51
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:01,919
What do you think?

52
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,740
Hmm, he only sliced your eyelid.

53
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:09,234
The actual eyeball itself is just fine.

54
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,517
Perhaps you should sit this one out.

55
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:14,477
I think we've all seen enough of
the bubble launcher for one day.

56
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:17,017
Watch and learn as I take
care of this one myself!

57
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:17,930
Jojo!

58
00:05:18,013 --> 00:05:19,468
Just calm down, Speedwagon.

59
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,560
This guy is asking for it.

60
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:24,777
It's time for me to show off the brand
new technique I've been working on.

61
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:25,690
What?

62
00:05:25,773 --> 00:05:27,678
Please allow me to introduce myself.

63
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:29,700
My name is Joseph Joestar.

64
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:33,904
And these are the hands known for
defeating your mate-son Viento.

65
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:43,017
I call this move my Hamon Clacker Volley.

66
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:47,571
I start off by filling these little
clacker balls here with a bit of Hummel.

67
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,060
Oh no!

68
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,977
JoJo, what the hell do
you think you're doing?

69
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:00,589
This is no time for games.

70
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:01,858
What are you doing?

71
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,237
Are you trying to disrespect
my friend by playing the fool?

72
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,500
Not intentionally.

73
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:08,360
I'm trying to be serious.

74
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:11,877
Caesar, I am truly sorry
for the loss of your friend.

75
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:14,520
I understand both your
pain and your anger.

76
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:15,990
Additionally,

77
00:06:16,073 --> 00:06:17,637
these guys may be the biggest group of

78
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:20,600
egotistical jackasses
I've ever seen in my life.

79
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,697
I may not be a master of this yet,

80
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:26,662
but I'll still knock you into next
Tuesday with my clacker volley.

81
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:33,677
I hate to admit it, but I know
that my harmon is relatively weak.

82
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:37,197
I'm pretty sure I can make up for what
I'm lacking with these steel clackers

83
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:40,537
if I can just break open your skin
even a little and fill you with harmon.

84
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:43,277
That should even up my
handicap, don't you think?

85
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,889
I can tell you're nervous.

86
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:46,420
Take that!

87
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,660
Well, that was fun.

88
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:58,018
Let us keep moving.

89
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:01,917
Apparently, the human race has
regressed rather than evolved.

90
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,412
Quite an understatement.

91
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:08,001
Amusing, though.

92
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,220
Jojo, what are you doing?

93
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:14,217
Your childish little games are
going to get us all killed!

94
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:18,006
He's playing coy, but this may
actually be the best Jojo's got.

95
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,997
He'd be fine if he was facing
some common street punk,

96
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:23,097
but I don't think he realizes that these

97
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:25,557
opponents are on a
completely different level.

98
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:28,280
It would be comical if
it weren't so tragic.

99
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:31,777
Why isn't anyone taking my
little metal balls seriously?

100
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:32,960
That's far enough!

101
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,057
Don't make me clack you into the ground!

102
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:35,970
Stop.

103
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,137
Don't you feel that human
lives are short enough?

104
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:41,177
There's no need to sprint to your death.

105
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:42,090
Silence!

106
00:07:42,173 --> 00:07:45,617
If you've ever had spaghetti on Nero
de Cepia, you know it looks bad,

107
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:46,818
but it's delicious.

108
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:50,195
You should taste my clacker
volley before you judge it!

109
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:57,060
The clackers, they vanished!

110
00:07:57,900 --> 00:08:03,740
I've been training on my
harmon all the live long day.

111
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:05,800
He's insane

112
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:10,920
Well, look at Mar, no hands.

113
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,553
Where are the clackers?

114
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:17,360
A true magician never reveals his secrets.

115
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,410
Ain't this

116
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:27,280
How can anything move like that?

117
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:29,117
I can't believe what I'm seeing.

118
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,797
He's faster than San Viento Jojo,

119
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:34,527
I don't think those idiotic
clackers did so much as graze him!

120
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:39,260
I admire your weapon, your courage,
and your creativity, human.

121
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:42,759
I'm actually enjoying your company.

122
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,140
You deserve time.

123
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,380
One minute.

124
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:46,980
But only one.

125
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:51,004
That is how much time I will allow
you to fight the mighty Wamuu.

126
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:54,610
Jojo!

127
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,340
I shall use your wound as a timer.

128
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,377
Your wrist will work well
as a timekeeping device,

129
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:04,989
and you will lose consciousness due to
a loss of blood in exactly one minute.

130
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,740
Show me what you can do, human.

131
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:12,513
This is what I often told the
members of the Hamon tribe.

132
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:16,040
Your life is now my
hourglass, measured in blood.

133
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,200
Wamu, we'll be waiting outside.

134
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:22,700
Now, boy, go ahead and retrieve
your weapon, quickly. What?

135
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:23,650
I'm sorry.

136
00:09:23,733 --> 00:09:25,417
I'm growing deaf in this ear.

137
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:29,400
It almost sounded like you said
go ahead and retrieve your weapon,

138
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:31,169
which would be ridiculous.

139
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:35,578
I mean, why would you retrieve
something that comes right back to you?

140
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:48,017
Looks like my clack of
boomerang worked pretty well.

141
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:51,453
I shouldn't even need the full
minute to destroy you now.

142
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:56,017
That's for killing Caesar's friend,
that's for not taking me seriously,

143
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:59,453
and that's because I'm sick
of looking at your ugly face!

144
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,020
Do what you must.

145
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,500
I deserve as much.

146
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:07,337
No opponent has ever struck my face, and
this is the price for my carelessness.

147
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:12,008
I shall take this beating in order to
properly honor you before I destroy you.

148
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:24,226
You say that no one has ever hit
you in that ugly mug of yours?

149
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:25,860
What an honor!

150
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:31,517
You didn't even stop to blink when you
killed Caesar's friend Mark, did you?

151
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,430
You monster!

152
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:34,520
Do you not value life at all?

153
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,400
Jojo, watch yourself!

154
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:39,640
His arm isn't broken, he's
getting ready to use it!

155
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:48,497
Whoa, I have a feeling
this isn't good for me.

156
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:51,040
A charming observation, human.

157
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,760
I'm now scarred due to my carelessness.

158
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:58,957
It was my duty to allow you to pummel me
as punishment for my own lack of judgment.

159
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,820
That has now ended, however.

160
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,572
JoJo, finish him now while you still can!

161
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,360
My ultimate technique!

162
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:07,960
The Divine Sandstorm!

163
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,364
I don't like the sound of that!

164
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:12,717
He starts by spinning
his left arm clockwise

165
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:15,397
and then his right arm counterclockwise.

166
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:18,537
JoJo is unprepared to
counter a technique like

167
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:21,620
this as Wamuu's fists seem
to grow before his eyes.

168
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:29,320
The air between Wamuu's arms transforms
into a powerful vortex of destruction.

169
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:33,251
This vacuum creates a highly
pressurized, deadly maelstrom.

170
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:38,137
Great, if he can tear
through marble pillars,

171
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:41,577
I don't see myself having much of a
chance against a windstorm like this.

172
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:44,719
I don't think I've ever
seen anything this powerful!

173
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,480
I call that divine sandstorm.

174
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:02,380
No! Jojo!

175
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:04,055
Don't be a damn fool!

176
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:05,420
Run, Speedwagon.

177
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:07,417
Get out of here before it's too late.

178
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,500
I'll try and distract him somehow.

179
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,748
Curse this blood in my eye.

180
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,750
Threw off my aim.

181
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:16,898
But it proved enough when you made
the choice to hide behind a pillar.

182
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:19,250
Hmm.

183
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:20,460
You died quickly.

184
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:24,989
Normally, I would ignore human
onlookers such as yourselves.

185
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:26,210
However,

186
00:12:26,293 --> 00:12:31,084
you witnessed my shame, so unfortunately
I must take the time to destroy you both.

187
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,320
You may pray now if you wish.

188
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,190
Huh?

189
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:42,730
Hmm.

190
00:12:42,813 --> 00:12:43,839
Must be the light.

191
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:50,000
What does he think he's doing?

192
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:52,080
I don't believe it.

193
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:54,104
He's actually trying to escape.

194
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:56,050
Huh?

195
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:58,070
Hmm.

196
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:03,760
That coward has no shame
playing dead like that.

197
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:05,640
I understand leaving me.

198
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,329
But what about Speedwagon?

199
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,017
I knew he was spineless.

200
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:12,820
This guy is the most
powerful foe I've ever faced.

201
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:14,864
My breathing is out of control.

202
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,740
I can't control my Hamon.

203
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:19,511
I don't really have any other option left.

204
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:22,620
Luckily, my specialty is running away.

205
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:26,817
Behold our now broken hero.

206
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,480
Jojo forced to play dead,

207
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:33,427
crawling for his life, and now leaving
Speedwagon behind to face certain death.

208
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:38,540
Even with all of this, Jojo remains
dedicated, a hero worthy of this tale.

209
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,335
How is that, you ask?

210
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:46,220
Nice try there, human!

211
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:48,780
You coward!

212
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:52,669
No true warrior would ever feign
death just to save himself!

213
00:13:56,920 --> 00:14:01,214
That may be true, though my intention
was not to escape, but to distract.

214
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:04,937
Truth be told, I was just trying
to get you onto this minecart.

215
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:06,397
You are clever indeed.

216
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,310
Indeed.

217
00:14:07,393 --> 00:14:10,777
So you were only playing the part of the
coward to lure me away from your friends,

218
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:11,690
is that right?

219
00:14:11,773 --> 00:14:13,157
I'm surprised you fell for it.

220
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,317
That trick is probably older than you.

221
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:17,200
Get out now, Speedwagon. Run!

222
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,480
Caesar, go!

223
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:20,112
What are you guys doing?

224
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:23,090
Chocho.

225
00:14:23,173 --> 00:14:24,003
That bastard.

226
00:14:24,086 --> 00:14:25,240
What a noble move.

227
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:28,137
Now that I've painted
myself into a corner here,

228
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:32,680
I need to come up with a second
part to my plan, which would be...

229
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:37,400
The unflappable hero.

230
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:40,697
He calmly searches for options,
not knowing what to do next.

231
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,580
But his will remains unbroken.

232
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:44,250
Jojo!

233
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:46,940
Damn you, Jojo!

234
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:49,480
He's in far worse shape than I am.

235
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:53,426
I should have been the
one to lure Wamuu away.

236
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:57,524
I see now that Jojo only acts
foolishly to confound his opponent.

237
00:14:57,740 --> 00:15:01,093
He must actually have a good
plan to beat those monsters.

238
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:12,557
Although you are quite confident for
someone who is knocking on death's door,

239
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:15,287
I must tell you that
your plan is a poor one.

240
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,657
You're quite tough, I'll give you that.

241
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,799
Soft-headed, but tough nonetheless.

242
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:24,317
Tell me, how do you remain unyielding
in the moments before your death?

243
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:28,457
Is it because you have bricks for brains,
or do you still have another trick for me?

244
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:32,200
Do you really want to know?
Actually, no. Let me guess.

245
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:34,417
Because you're so obviously clever,

246
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:36,517
I'll give you the benefit of
the doubt that you wouldn't be

247
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:40,037
stupid enough to be holding a
stick of dynamite behind your back.

248
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,296
Damn, he's on to me!

249
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:44,597
And I know you wouldn't insult my
intelligence by thinking you could

250
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,677
quickly throw the brake and send
the mine cart flying off the tracks.

251
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:48,740
Maybe like this!

252
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:54,349
Damn, he got me there too!

253
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:01,757
The time on your hourglass
wrist is just about up.

254
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:05,840
There is absolutely no chance that
you will survive this any longer.

255
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:09,155
I found your tricks to be very quaint.

256
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:15,200
Before you die, tell me, why do I
still not see defeat in your eyes?

257
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:19,577
I'll tell you if you want, but you're
gonna have to say please first.

258
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:20,490
More games!

259
00:16:20,573 --> 00:16:21,917
You've tested me long enough.

260
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,860
Prepare to die! Such a shame,

261
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:28,549
because a month from now I can guarantee
that I would be able to destroy you.

262
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,350
What was that?

263
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:34,988
With just one more month of
training, I would annihilate you.

264
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:39,177
I was the first person to hit as
well as the first to scar your face.

265
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:43,436
When I put my mind to something, I
can accomplish pretty much anything.

266
00:16:45,660 --> 00:16:48,601
Oh, well, I guess none of
that really matters now.

267
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:51,240
So, can we just get this over with?

268
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:55,874
It will be an honor to be killed by
a warrior like you, blah, blah, blah.

269
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,191
What do you mean by this?

270
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:00,777
Oh, I'm sick and tired
of all this talking.

271
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:04,340
Just hurry up and make it
painless, Wamu. Explain yourself.

272
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:06,425
What are you trying to get at?

273
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:16,720
I don't know how, but he's still alive.

274
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:20,694
Is it true that you pillar
men often live for millennia?

275
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:22,977
That's a long time to be
walking around with the

276
00:17:23,060 --> 00:17:26,236
shame of having your face
rearranged by a lowly human.

277
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:29,857
It seems to me that the only way
you could regain your honor would be

278
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:33,817
by defeating me in a fight after I've
undergone proper Harmon training.

279
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:37,320
I do not have to defeat you
in order to maintain my honor.

280
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:40,540
His entire body is shaking with rage.

281
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:44,137
I have a chance if I can make him
think his integrity is at stake.

282
00:17:44,220 --> 00:17:48,817
He gave himself away as the proud warrior
type the moment he called me a coward.

283
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:50,547
Pride is his Achilles' heel.

284
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:53,537
I don't know if you noticed,
but I'm still new at this.

285
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,450
However,

286
00:17:54,533 --> 00:17:56,097
if I trained with my Harmon for a month,

287
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:59,517
I know I could give you the fair
fight a warrior like you deserves.

288
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:03,117
The first person who ever hit you
in the face gave you a nasty scar.

289
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:07,024
It would be a shame if you killed
that person before he's worthy.

290
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:10,477
But if you feel the need to kill me before

291
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:12,657
I have a chance to battle you as an equal,

292
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:15,387
then go ahead and do
whatever you need to do.

293
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:18,790
You bastard!

294
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:20,970
Bamu.

295
00:18:21,053 --> 00:18:21,883
Master ACDC.

296
00:18:21,966 --> 00:18:23,400
You gave this human one minute.

297
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:26,464
Why must you insist on
letting him toy with you?

298
00:18:26,780 --> 00:18:27,920
Just go away!

299
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,100
I almost had him!

300
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:44,640
Master ACDC, I have grown fond of this
particular member of the Hamon tribe.

301
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:46,360
I got him!

302
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:51,197
Jojo, you will be happy to know that I
have decided to accept your proposition.

303
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:54,437
If you swear that you will train your
hardest to fulfill your potential,

304
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:57,297
then I will give you
exactly one month to do so.

305
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:59,397
So you're not going to kill me now?

306
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,310
That's right.

307
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:03,180
But we're going to fight again. We are.

308
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,237
Are you sure you want to do this?

309
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,377
I'll give you a chance to take it back.

310
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:08,290
Yes.

311
00:19:08,373 --> 00:19:09,826
I can't believe it's working.

312
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:15,182
However, I will need assurances that you
will not try to run away again, of course.

313
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:17,020
Nice, Wamu.

314
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:19,057
I was wondering when you
would finally propose.

315
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:21,760
Say hello to the wedding ring of death.

316
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,296
Guess where it goes?

317
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:25,200
A hint, not on your finger.

318
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,880
What are you doing with that?

319
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:33,340
This ring will start
to dissolve in 33 days.

320
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,420
It's impossible to remove.

321
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:38,916
And once dissolved, it will
release a virulent poison.

322
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:43,356
Any attempt to remove or damage it
will also release the lethal poison.

323
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:49,020
However, there is one certain way
to dissolve the ring without harm.

324
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:51,920
Simply battle and defeat
me within 33 days,

325
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:56,557
and I shall give you the antidote that
I keep inside the hollow of my lip ring.

326
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,470
Jojo!

327
00:19:57,553 --> 00:20:01,300
The vow on that wedding ring
states, till death do us part, Jojo.

328
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:05,100
Be at the Coliseum in 33 days,
meet me there at midnight,

329
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:07,438
and we shall battle as equals, Jojo.

330
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:12,637
I hope you didn't think your poultry
tricks would help you escape, human.

331
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:17,544
I don't imagine the two of us will fight,
but just in case, here's a gift for you.

332
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:21,060
One that fits perfectly
around your windpipe!

333
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,980
My heart and my throat!

334
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:27,877
My poison is quite different from Wammu's.

335
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:31,254
And I keep the antidote for
that poison in my nose ring.

336
00:20:32,020 --> 00:20:34,520
Kars, would you like to go next?

337
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:35,800
I don't think so.

338
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:38,599
Immortality can be boring at times.

339
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:43,720
To encounter a worthy opponent, that is
both such a rare and tantalizing thought.

340
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:46,452
A gift that would give our lives meaning.

341
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:48,480
I can see why you do this.

342
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:52,337
However, do not forget that our goal
is to obtain the Red Stone of Asia.

343
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:53,655
We must stay focused.

344
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:54,950
Let's go.

345
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:59,680
Train long and hard, Jojo, so you
can challenge my divine sandstorm.

346
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:05,260
I can't believe that.

347
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:07,285
Two wedding rings with poison?

348
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:10,137
Is that supposed to be some
kind of sick joke or something?

349
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:13,097
I've got one around my throat
and one around my heart.

350
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:16,533
Do these guys think I'm some
kind of bigamist or maybe...

351
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:23,460
Well, at least Speedwagon
and Caesar are safe.

352
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:25,172
That's what's important.

353
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,780
No sense in feeling sorry for myself.

354
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,160
Jojo, you fool.

355
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:40,500
That was one hell of a
bluff you just pulled there.

356
00:21:40,980 --> 00:21:43,637
The best con man couldn't
have done it better than you.

357
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:47,840
You acted bravely, but now
you'll need to back it up.

358
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:53,280
We don't have much time to work, and
we have serious Haman training ahead.

359
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:02,120
In and around the lake,
mountains come out of the sky.

360
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:05,180
They stand there,

361
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:10,020
24 before my love, I'll be there.

362
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:24,460
guitar solo

363
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:31,957
When I said I needed a month,
I only meant it as a blurb!

364
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:34,157
Well, from up here, it's
really more deep than tall.

365
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,070
God, wait!

366
00:23:35,153 --> 00:23:35,983
Please don't do this!

367
00:23:36,066 --> 00:23:38,457
Because you're a girl, doesn't mean
that I won't give you what you deserve.

368
00:23:38,540 --> 00:23:39,599
Welcome to Venice.
